|[[File:item_884.png|link=]] [[Lightweight Bag]]
|[[File:Iridium_18x18.png|link=]] 500
|This lightweight bag will hold 12 items at 100% weight reduction.  Perfect for heavy lifting on your travels.  This item cannot be traded and is bound to the character you purchased it on.
|-
|[[File:item_1444.png|link=]] [[Spacious Rucksack]]
|[[File:Iridium_18x18.png|link=]] 750
|This lightweight rucksack will hold 24 items at 80% weight reduction.  Perfect for the adventurer who needs to hold just a little bit more, and doesn't mind a bit of lift.  This items cannot be traded, and is bound to the character you purchased it on.
|-
|[[File:item_5910.png|link=]] [[Storage Trunk]]
|[[File:Iridium_18x18.png|link=]] 1000
|This weighted trunk will hold 50 items.  It provides no weight reductions, weights 50 stones, and is fairly heavy!  Your character may be weighed down after purchasing it.  Any contents in the Trunk will be considerably heavier.  Perfect for the adventurer who banks frequently.  This item cannot be traded, and is bound to the character you purchased it on.
|}

== Cosmetics ==

{| class="wikitable"
|+
!Item
!Iridium Cost
!Description
|-
|[[File:item_5797.png|link=]] [[Armor Ornamentation Token]]
|[[File:Iridium_18x18.png|link=]] 500
|This token can be merged into a piece of visible armor to copy its appearance into the form of an Armor Ornamentation Exaltation.  This does not destroy the item you are copying the appearance from.  WARNING: Does not work on Robe items.  The Token and generated Ornamentation cannot be traded, and can only be used on the character you purchase the Token on.
|-
|[[File:item_5791.png|link=]] [[Robe Ornamentation Token]]
|[[File:Iridium_18x18.png|link=]] 1000
|This token can be merged into a piece of visible robe (chest) armor to copy its appearance into the form of a Robe Ornamentation Exaltation.  This does not destroy the item you are copying the appearance from.  WARNING: Does not work on other types of armor.  The Token and the generated Ornamentation cannot be traded, and can only be used on the character you purchase the Token on.
|-
|[[File:item_5864.png|link=]] [[Weapon Ornamentation Token]]
|[[File:Iridium_18x18.png|link=]] 750
|This token can be merged into a weapon to copy its appearance into the form of a Weapon Ornamentation Exaltation.  This does not destroy the item you are copying the appearance from.  Primary and Secondary only Weapons can be used in either hand.  This also applies to other items, such as Shields and Symbols.  The Token and the generated Ornamentation cannot be traded, and can only be used on the character you purchase the Token on.
|}

== Items ==

{| class="wikitable"
|+
!Item
!Iridium Cost
!Description
|-
|[[File:item_2045.png|link=]] [[Bottle of Alternate Adventure]]
|[[File:Iridium_18x18.png|link=]] 500
|Consumable potion that applies a buff with 5 charges to your current character.  When you gain an Alternate Adventure Point, you will gain an additional Point and consume on charge.  This effect can be applied to the player multiple times to increase the amount of charges.  This potion lasts forever and persists through death, loadout swap and cannot be dispelled.  This item cannot be traded, and is bound to the character you have purchased it on.
|}

== Mounts ==

{| class="wikitable"
|+
!Item
!Iridium Cost
!Description
|-
|[[File:item_1634.png|link=]] [[Bristly Boar Reins]]
|[[File:Iridium_18x18.png|link=]] 1500
|Summons a Bristly Boar mount.  This mount increases your run speed and let's you travel around Norrath in boarish style.  This mount's default run speed is roughly equivalent to Spirit of the Wolf and, like all mounts, its speed will increase to the highest level of any summoned mount you unlock on your character.  This Mount cannot be traded and is bound to the character you have purchased it on.
|}

